    <name>Appbase BOM</name>
    <description>Bill of Materials — importable dependencyManagement pinning every publishable Appbase module to this release's version</description>

    <!--
    Consumers import this once:

        <dependencyManagement>
            <dependencies>
                <dependency>
                    <groupId>com.viveworks.appbase</groupId>
                    <artifactId>appbase-bom</artifactId>
                    <version>1.0.0</version>
                    <type>pom</type>
                    <scope>import</scope>
                </dependency>
            </dependencies>
        </dependencyManagement>

    ...then declare any Appbase dependency without a <version> — this
    BOM supplies it, so every Appbase artifact a consumer pulls in is
    from the same coherent release.

    Only leaf (packaging=jar) modules are listed — aggregator/pom-packaging
    modules (appbase-client, appbase-service, appbase-bootstrap, appbase-java)
    produce no artifact of their own and aren't consumable dependencies.

    Release 1 also leaves OUT the leaf modules the lean baseline defers
    (Release 1.0 Lean Requirements baseline, reconciled 2026-08-28, §4.2/§4.3):
      appbase-client-clamav, appbase-client-smtp, appbase-client-jasync,
      appbase-client-spark,
    and, by the owner's internal work item 1141 Q1 ruling (2026-09-27), appbase-service-user-account-r2dbc.
    A BOM entry is a publication claim, and those are not supported. The single
    list is scripts/test/release1-excluded-artifacts.txt; bom_release1_test.sh
    derives the expected set from the reactor and fails on any drift, in both
    directions, and when this comment disagrees with the list.
    -->
